extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 149-151 (cache p149-p151, page_offset 0). The class opens at the foot of printed 149; lore, the stat block and abilities 1-4 are printed 150, the rest printed 151. Printed 150 read off a 110 dpi render: the OCR''s ''1.Q.'' is I.Q. 3D6+8, and the stray colon after Spd. 5D6 is not on the page. || XP: the Neo-Human ladder, printed 192, as briefed. || ATTRIBUTES as printed. || POOLS: 4D6x10 S.D.C. and P.E. x3 hit points, +2D6 hit points per level, stored as sdc_base / hit_points_base because the R.C.C. is the character''s whole class (its own skills and related list), so no men_of_arms line. The book''s M.D.C. line reads ''See psionic powers'': the Supernatural Transformation turns S.D.C. and hit points into M.D.C. only while it lasts, so mdc_from_hp_sdc is NOT set - that flag is a permanent conversion, and the transformation is temporary and ends when the I.S.P. base runs out (the Psycho-Stalker''s Bio-Feedback, an I.S.P.-bought temporary conversion, is stored the same way, as an ability). No mdc_base. P.P.E. 2D6. || PSIONICS: master (the book likens them to a Mind Melter and the Mind-Wave text names master psionics). I.S.P. 1D4x100 plus M.E., +12 per level. Three powers from each of the four categories including Super at creation (powers_starting 12 as four groups); ''with the same restrictions as a Mind Melter'' is read as the Mind Melter''s rule that Mind Wipe, Psi-Sword and Mentally Possess Others are unavailable before level 3 (Rifts Ultimate Edition, as the mind-melter class records it), so the Super group and the level-2 Super pick exclude those three by catalog name. The Mind Melter''s four automatic powers are not granted - the page grants restrictions, not powers. Level 2: four powers, one from each category. Level 3: three from any category. Each later level: two from any, written out as schedule entries 4-15. The five numbered abilities are this page''s own powers, not catalog rows (Hyper-Telekinesis is not Telekinesis (Super)), so they are special_abilities, never stubbed psionic powers. || BONUSES stored: +1 initiative, +1 save vs magic (spell_magic), +3 save vs possession, +3 vs mind control, +6 vs Horror Factor. Horror Factor 9 stored as horror_factor; the book qualifies it as applying when identity and powers are revealed, noted in the ability. || SKILLS: Language and Literacy: Spanish (98%) as Language: Spanish 98 plus Literacy: Native Language 98, this book''s convention. Language: one of choice (+15%) is a Language: Other pick. Radio Basic is Radio: Basic 45+10. Intelligence 32+10 (per level 4). Disguise 25+10. W.P. Energy Rifle plus two W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts or Assassin for one other skill; no alignment condition printed. || RELATED: five plus one at levels 3, 5, 7, 10 and 14. Communications, Domestic, Medical, Rogue, Technical and Wilderness +5; Espionage and Pilot +10; Electrical, Mechanical, Military, Physical, Pilot Related, Science and W.P. any. Horsemanship and Cowboy are not printed and not granted. SECONDARY: two each at levels 1, 5 and 10. || EQUIPMENT: energy rifle of choice - the Achilles Lightbringer (printed 165) or the usual Rifts laser rifles; energy sidearm of choice - the IP-7 (Achilles militia, printed 163) or the usual pistols; e-clip x8 (four each). Choice of human-type body armor, usually light (M.D.C. 45 to 60): a choice among catalog suits in that band - gaucho-combat-armor 45 and battle-infantry-armor 60 from this book, huntsman 45, urban warrior 50 and bushman 60. walkie-talkie for the hand radio, food-rations for one week''s rations, gas-mask, survival-kit, bedroll, survival-knife. || MONEY: 2D6x100 credits. || No Cybernetics line is printed and none is stored. Experience: the book says player characters should start at first level (not first or second, as the Condoroid and Falconoid say). Alignment: any - GM notes."
---

## Lore

In Project Achilles'' last years rival teams worked in secret against one
another, and when the felinoid team announced its success, one faction
decided that animals were the wrong starting point and set out to improve
humans directly. They altered human embryos, fast-cloned with genetic material
taken from center staff without their consent, chasing the genes tied to
psychic power. Researcher Cordelia Valdez discovered the work and found that
most of the embryos carried her own genes; resolving to save these children,
she staged the escape that saved the Republic''s founders.

The neo-humans look entirely human and physically near-flawless, sharp of
mind and senses, and hold perhaps the greatest psychic power of any engineered
race - strength to fight a tank bare-handed, the power to heal, and the power
to kill with a thought. They age barely at all, and the survivors are nearly
three centuries old. After the Rifts they split: the Neo-Abels stayed with the
mutant animals and serve Achilles as agents, special forces and champions,
while the Neo-Cains left in contempt for the lesser races and have not been
seen since.

The Republic values them and mistrusts them. That the mightiest mutants look
human galls the animal mutants, rivalry is constant, and rumors blame the
Cain-brood for every misfortune. A few neo-humans have left to travel the
Megaverse among demigods, dragons, Cosmo-Knights and True Atlanteans.

## GM Notes

Alignment: any. Neo-humans get along best with mutant capybaras and worst with
serpentoids, and often befriend Mind Melters, master Blood Riders, godlings,
demigods and other powerful beings.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'neo-human');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'neo-human';

